  ('581800191632137917', 'Scrooge: A Christmas Carol', 2022, 'Animation, Family, Fantasy', 'Stephen Donnelly', 'Leslie Bricusse, Stephen Donnelly', 'Luke Evans, Olivia Colman, Jessie Buckley, Johnny Flynn, Fra Fee, Giles Terera, Trevor Dion Nicholas, James Cosmo', 'G', 'On a cold Christmas Eve, selfish miser Ebenezer Scrooge has one night left to face his past — and change the future — before time runs out.', 'On a cold Christmas Eve, selfish miser Ebenezer Scrooge has one night left to face his past — and change the future — before time runs out.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/oyGb5JpEYMEqDDjfJKLEvPTVSjK.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:1001865'),
  ('654810735138406168', 'Scrooged', 1988, 'Fantasy, Comedy, Drama', 'Richard Donner, Michael Chapman, Gabriela Vázquez', 'Mitch Glazer, Michael O''Donoghue', 'Bill Murray, Karen Allen, John Forsythe, John Glover, Bobcat Goldthwait, Robert Mitchum, David Johansen, Carol Kane', 'PG-13', 'Frank Cross is a wildly successful television executive whose cold ambition and curmudgeonly nature has driven away the love of his life. But after firing a staff member on Christmas Eve, Frank is visited by a series of ghosts who give him a chance to re-evaluate his actions and right the wrongs of his past.', 'Frank Cross is a wildly successful television executive whose cold ambition and curmudgeonly nature has driven away the love of his life. But after firing a staff member on Christmas Eve, Frank is visited by a series of ghosts who give him a chance to re-evaluate his actions and right the wrongs of his past.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/uO0znfB2ZzTXA1IS7jkrjNbpkYK.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:9647'),
  ('635956583990625985', 'Scrub Me Mama with a Boogie Beat', 1941, 'Comedy, Animation, Family', 'Walter Lantz', null, 'Ivie Anderson, Mel Blanc', null, 'Lazy black folks in Lazy Town (Pop. 123½) are napping and attracting flies. They are so lethargic they even fight in slow motion. Then a riverboat arrives with a red hot mama on board. Faster than you can say "Jim Crow", she has everyone moving to a Harlem boogie beat, dancing, scrubbing clothes, and eating watermelon. As the boogie-woogie comes to a close, Mammy hoists her skirt. Her big bottom reads "The End".', 'Lazy black folks in Lazy Town (Pop. 123½) are napping and attracting flies. They are so lethargic they even fight in slow motion. Then a riverboat arrives with a red hot mama on board. Faster than you can say "Jim Crow", she has everyone moving to a Harlem boogie beat, dancing, scrubbing clothes, and eating watermelon. As the boogie-woogie comes to a close, Mammy hoists her skirt. Her big bottom reads "The End".', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/736X30KLPGeNagKiVjtrDNVY5SE.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:236547'),
